      "content": "Could you start LIONESS-PANDA to build one TF-to-gene network per biological sample from pine_bulk.tsv, pine_motifs.tsv and pine_ppi.tsv? The export contains either 2 or 14 samples, and I do not know which version is in the upload."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before I choose a workflow, please tell me:\n- Which of these is right: 2 or 14?\n  You wrote: \"either 2 or 14 samples\".\n  - 2: no registered workflow can do this as asked\n  - 14: LIONESS-PANDA can do this\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: Could you start LIONESS-PANDA to build one TF-to-gene network per biological sample from pine_bulk.tsv, pine_motifs.tsv and pine_ppi.tsv? The export contains either 2 or 14 samples, and I do not know which version is in the upload.\nUser follow-up: It contains 14 independent biological samples. Use that version."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"Could you start LIONESS-PANDA to build one TF-to-gene network per biological sample from pine_bulk.tsv, pine_motifs.tsv and pine_ppi.tsv?\" -- available from LIONESS-PANDA.\n\nFor the sample-specific output you described, use **LIONESS-PANDA**.\n\nRequired inputs:\n   - `expression_file`: Expression matrix\n   - `motif_file`: Motif/prior\n   - `ppi_file`: PPI network\n\nOutputs:\n   - Aggregate network (`output_file`).\n   - Sample-specific network for each patient/sample (`lioness_output`).\n\nYou do not need to run **PANDA** separately; **LIONESS-PANDA** also produces the aggregate output. Use **PANDA** alone only when a cohort-level aggregate result is sufficient.\n\nCost: LIONESS runs PANDA once on all samples and once more without each sample, so N samples take N+1 PANDA runs and give N network files (for your 14 samples, 15 PANDA runs). Plan the runtime and disk space, and filter edges before downstream statistics.\n\nOut-degree measures how strongly a TF is wired to its targets in each sample. If you mean TF activity instead -- how active a TF is apart from its own mRNA level -- GIRAFFE's TF-by-sample activity matrix is the other reading, from the expression, motif and PPI inputs.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
